From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 3 AVPs from 3GPP TS 29.338
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3GPP TS 29.338 V18.2.0 defines these AVPs in vendor 10415, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  HSS-ID (3325): UTF8String, clause 6.3.3.14
  Originating-SIP-URI (3326): UTF8String, clause 6.3.3.15
  OFR-Flags (3328): Unsigned32, clause 6.3.3.12

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml
index 65e5a13..220788c 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml
@@ -1525,6 +1525,15 @@
     <avp name="RDR-Flags" code="3323" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
       <type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
     </avp>
+    <avp name="HSS-ID" code="3325" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+      <type type-name="UTF8String"/>
+    </avp>
+    <avp name="Originating-SIP-URI" code="3326" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+      <type type-name="UTF8String"/>
+    </avp>
+    <avp name="OFR-Flags" code="3328" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+      <type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
+    </avp>
 
     <avp name="Maximum-UE-Availability-Time" code="3329" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
       <type type-name="Time"/>
